            <ArticleTitle>Pharmacological management of pain and infection in the surgical oncology patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-96</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Surgical oncology patients are often high-risk patients that require careful perioperative management for a successful outcome. Prophylactic antibiotics are needed to prevent infection in tissues compromised by disease, radiation, or chemotherapy. Pain control is needed to prevent the stress response to surgery from worsening the outcome and to aid in the maintenance of patient comfort.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
